{
  "rationale": "The model separates sensing from motion capability and uses small deterministic specifications to bind each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. Clear conditions strongly favor forward progress via move_forward and occasional brief random_walk. Obstacle conditions always enter dedicated recovery states: front obstacles trigger a one-shot backward escape, left obstacles trigger clockwise turning, and right obstacles trigger counterclockwise turning. A small post-back decision layer returns to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed, while allowing a sparse full_rotate only as a last-resort blocked recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use one sensor plant and one motion-capability plant, then encode policy in specifications with perception states and one-shot action states.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, allow occasional random_walk through a separate clear-mode alternation spec, and keep obstacle recovery conservative and short."
  ],
